"answer": "Regular prenatal checkups are important because they help keep both the mother and baby healthy and allow providers to spot problems early [MLP-6057, MLP-6]. Even when a problem cannot be treated before birth, early detection is beneficial because it gives parents time to learn about the baby's condition and prepare for any challenges they may face after the baby is born [MLP-6057, MLP-3091]. Additionally, checkups help prevent problems during delivery, such as identifying a breech position that might require a Cesarean section to avoid complications [MLP-6057]."
